# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
#
# How to cite SPMD IR. GitHub turns this file into the "Cite this
# repository" button; it offers the preferred-citation below. Cite the
# first SPMD IR paper (the preferred-citation) for SPMD IR in general;
# for a specific feature or extension, cite the paper in `references`
# that introduced it. `references` also lists work built on SPMD IR (its
# `notes` say so). Add new papers to `references`, newest last.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SPMD IR, or refer to it in general, please cite the first
  SPMD IR paper below. If you build on, or refer to, a specific feature or
  extension, cite the paper that introduced it instead (see the
  references).
title: SPMD IR
type: software
abstract: >-
  An MLIR dialect and toolchain for statically verifying and optimising
  SPMD (single-program, multiple-data) parallel programs -- data races,
  collective-communication mismatches, thread-safety violations and more
  -- across MPI, OpenSHMEM, NVSHMEM, NCCL, CUDA and OpenMP.
authors:
  - given-names: Semih
    family-names: Burak
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6048-9643"
repository-code: "https://github.com/spmd-ir/spmd"
url: "https://github.com/spmd-ir"
# CFF accepts only plain SPDX identifiers, not "Apache-2.0 WITH
# LLVM-exception". The exception only adds permissions, so Apache-2.0 is
# accurate; license-url points to the full terms.
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/spmd-ir/spmd/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
keywords:
  - MLIR
  - SPMD
  - MPI
  - OpenSHMEM
  - NVSHMEM
  - NCCL
  - CUDA
  - OpenMP
  - static analysis
  - correctness checking
